# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# AutoModz environment - the deployment checklist.
#
# This file is the list somebody copies when they set the product up, so a key
# the code READS and this file does not NAME is a feature that silently does
# not exist in production. `__tests__/deploy/configuration.test.ts` asserts the
# two lists agree; the sections below say what breaks when each is absent.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── 1. Firebase web app config (REQUIRED) ──────────────────────────────────
# Firebase console → Project settings (gear icon) → General → Your apps → Web app
# Without these: nobody can sign in.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Email that becomes admin on first sign-in.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_EMAIL=hello.automodz@gmail.com

# The site's own address, used for canonical URLs, the sitemap and every
# shareable link (an invoice, a chapter). Without it those links point at
# whatever host answered, which for a preview deployment is the preview.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://automodz.vercel.app

# ── 2. Firebase Admin SDK (REQUIRED) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Firebase console → Project settings → Service accounts → Generate new private key.
# Copy from the downloaded JSON; keep the \n characters in the private key.
#
# EVERY CUSTOMER ROOM RENDERS ON THE SERVER, so without these the product
# cannot mint a session cookie and every screen shows "your car is behind a
# sign-in" to a customer who is signed in.
FIREBASE_ADMIN_PROJECT_ID=
FIREBASE_ADMIN_CLIENT_EMAIL=
FIREBASE_ADMIN_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ── 3. Web push (OPTIONAL, free) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Firebase console → Project settings → Cloud Messaging → Web Push certificates
# → Generate key pair. Without it, notifications reach the app but not the
# phone's lock screen.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=

# ── 4. Images - Cloudinary, SIGNED (REQUIRED for any upload) ───────────────
# cloudinary.com → free account → Dashboard shows the cloud name, API key and
# API secret.
#
# THE UPLOAD PRESET IS GONE, and deliberately: it was UNSIGNED and shipped in
# the public bundle, so the cloud name and permission to write to it were
# public - anyone who opened devtools could fill the studio's account, and
# unsigned uploads cannot be deleted either. Every upload is now signed by the
# server for one exact `public_id` (`/api/media/sign`), which needs the secret.
#
# Without the three server-side values, `/api/media/sign` answers 503 and no
# photograph - a certificate, a car, a sell request - can be uploaded at all.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=

# ── 5. The nightly job (REQUIRED) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Any long random string. Vercel Cron sends it as the Authorization bearer.
#
# IT FAILS CLOSED. An unset secret leaves `/api/cron/daily` refusing every
# request, which means: no retention reminders, no membership expiry, no stale
# bookings aged out, and no daily figures. The alternative - running without a
# secret - would leave a public GET that fans push notifications out to every
# customer on the books, so closed is right and the key is not optional.
CRON_SECRET=

# ── 6. Payments & contact ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The studio's collecting UPI address. The customer's app opens with the
# STUDIO's figure already in it (design screen 13) - there is no gateway, and
# the studio confirms against the credit before a car is released.
# A malformed value is treated as none: the app then says it is not taking UPI
# and the customer settles at the counter, which is honest. Never a link to
# nowhere.
NEXT_PUBLIC_UPI_ID=automodz@upi
# Overrides the above when the collecting address must not be public.
STUDIO_UPI_VPA=
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=919512605088

# ── 7. WhatsApp Cloud API (OPTIONAL) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Leave empty to keep using free wa.me tap-to-send links (default).
# developers.facebook.com → create app → WhatsApp → API Setup.
WHATSAPP_TOKEN=
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=

# ── 8. Error reporting (OPTIONAL) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# A Sentry DSN. Without it, `reportError` logs to the server console only.
SENTRY_DSN=
